    "The biggest investment you will EVER make (and NEVER regret) is ALWAYS value your health and happiness more than ALL THE MONEY IN THE WORLD. NEVER let chasing after ANY AMOUNT of wealth take that from you, EVER.": "你一生中最重要、也最不会后悔的投资，是始终把健康与幸福看得比世间所有财富更重。无论追求多少财富，都不要以此为代价。",
    "ALWAYS have a future plan in place, of what you will buy / sell: 1) Around a certain future date in time. 2) If a certain price target has been met or exceeded. This doesn't need to be \"all in\" or \"all out\". For instance, you may want to split your capital gains between 2 tax years within a tight time period, in late December / early the following January, to avoid higher tax brackets.": "提前为未来的买卖制定计划：一是在某个日期前后采取什么行动，二是在达到或超过某个目标价格时如何操作。不必一次性全部买入或卖出。例如，你可能考虑在 12 月底和次年 1 月初分批实现资本收益，使其分布在两个纳税年度，以避免进入更高税率档。",
    "The \"grass on the other side looks greener\" MORE OFTEN THAN NOT will always be in your head, when you see other assets performing better than the ones you currently are holding. That's why it's SO IMPORTANT TO DO YOUR REASEARCH FULLY! If you KNOW you didn't buy garbage, AND you didn't over-extend your position (you CAN afford to hold it for a few years without selling any), just RELAX AND DON'T BE GREEDY...otherwise you are living for money (not ENJOYING life itself) AND YOU WILL END UP FLIPPING YOURSELF OUT, WHICH IS A CRAPPY WAY TO LIVE!": "当其他资产表现优于自己的持仓时，“这山望着那山高”的念头很容易冒出来。这正是充分研究如此重要的原因。如果你知道自己买的并非劣质资产，仓位也未超出承受能力，能在不卖出的情况下持有几年，那就放松些，不要贪心。否则，生活只剩下追逐金钱，而不是享受生活本身，最终只会让自己焦虑不堪。",
